{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 3, "text": "I have completed a full review of the provided patent application drafts against the inventor's source materials. The review covered the claims, detailed description, numerals, figure briefs, and formalities, checking for both source fidelity and internal consistency. While the draft is largely faithful to the source, I found one critical issue where the draft asserts a specific mechanical arrangement that is not described by the inventor, and a major issue where a claim recites a feature not supported by the disclosure.\n\nMy review process traced every numbered part, claim limitation, and structural or functional statement in the draft back to an affirmative statement in the `input/disclosure.md` or the USER sections of `input/conversation.md`. I also verified that terminology was used consistently, section lines were correctly referenced, and no drafting notes or placeholders remain. The following findings detail the unsupported assertions that must be corrected before filing."}
